# SURYA-MED – System Architecture

## 1. Overview

SURYA-MED follows a modular architecture integrating renewable energy generation, battery storage, energy monitoring and intelligent power distribution.

## 2. System Components

### A. Energy Generation

* Solar photovoltaic panel.
* Converts solar energy into electrical energy.

### B. Energy Storage

* Solar charge controller.
* Rechargeable battery.
* Battery protection system.

### C. Energy Monitoring

* Voltage sensors.
* Current sensors.
* Battery status monitoring.
* Individual load monitoring.

### D. Intelligent Control

* ESP32 / Arduino microcontroller.
* Sensor data processing.
* Battery-level evaluation.
* Priority-based energy management.

### E. Output and Display

* OLED/LCD display.
* LED indicators.
* Switching modules.
* Low-energy warning system.

## 3. System Data Flow

Solar Panel
↓
Solar Charge Controller
↓
Battery Storage
↓
Voltage and Current Sensors
↓
ESP32 / Arduino Controller
↓
Priority-Based Energy Allocation
↓
Switching Modules
↓
Selected Demonstration Loads

## 4. Monitoring Interface

The display provides:

* Battery level.
* Input voltage.
* Current consumption.
* Individual load status.
* Energy availability.
* Low-battery warnings.

## 5. System Operation

The controller continuously monitors energy availability and compares it against predefined thresholds.

When battery energy decreases, the controller disconnects lower-priority demonstration loads first.

Higher-priority demonstration loads remain connected while sufficient safe operating energy is available.


**Note:** This is a proposed architecture. Hardware integration and validation are planned development activities.
